From c969c73c662d76cac75c466494a422f14a2f6e96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HelaFaye <dilsha21@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 05:32:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] esp32s3: GP-SPI2/3 masters with GDMA; pin-link to wire
 boards

GP-SPI2 (0x60024000) and GP-SPI3 (0x60025000) were missing. Each now
has an SSI bus (spi2, spi3) and runs master transactions as ESP-IDF's
spi_ll drives them: command, address, dummy and data phases, W0-W15 or
GDMA (SPI2/SPI3 peripheral channels), full or half duplex, bit order,
CS0-5 per MISC (polarity, keep-active). TRANS_DONE comes after the
bits' time at the configured clock, with ETS_SPI2/3_INTR_SOURCE.

Chip selects are the FSPICSn/SPI3_CSn signals into the GPIO matrix, or
the IO_MUX for SPI2's own pins (GPIO9-14, function 4), so a device is
selected by its pin, whether the controller or the firmware drives it.

esp32s3.pin-link wires a pin to a device's GPIO line from the command
line (in, out, open drain, board pull resistor, invert); the GPIO model
gains pin-pull inputs and listeners so several devices can follow a pin.
